From 4776c6add86e144ae4ba7c90f4ce58b4ca51f055 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:25:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 19/94] pmdomain: qcom: cpr3: add SDM630/SDM660 CPRh

Add the SDM630/660 CPRh data: two threads (power and performance
cluster), their fuse layout, corner voltages and scaling factors, from
the HiBy RS6 stock 1.80 kernel and the vendor cprh-kbss-regulator.c, and
the qcom,sdm660-cprh compatible.

qcom_cpr_cpu_pd_index() finds the CPR domain of a CPU by the "cpr" name
in power-domain-names, so the PSCI domain can come first. Build
cpr-common.o and cpr3.o as one module so that QCOM_CPR3=m works.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SXjPGasJxD6XRYU1J9jsnW
